   "id": "WTrVfTxflfUh",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "WTrVfTxflfUh"
   },
   "source": [
    "## 15. Hyperparameter Tuning — Best Two Real Models\n",
    "\n",
    "The Dummy baseline is **not** tuned. The two best non-dummy models by CV RMSE are tuned.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "IKEYT7wXlfUh",
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "id": "IKEYT7wXlfUh",
    "outputId": "288331d8-667e-4af5-ac89-c6fc7faf3c5e"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "search_spaces = {\n",
    "    \"Linear Regression\": {\n",
    "        \"model__fit_intercept\": [True, False],\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"Ridge\": {\n",
    "        \"model__alpha\": np.logspace(-3, 3, 25),\n",
    "        \"model__fit_intercept\": [True, False],\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"Lasso\": {\n",
    "        \"model__alpha\": np.logspace(-4, 2, 25),\n",
    "        \"model__fit_intercept\": [True, False],\n",
    "        \"model__max_iter\": [10_000, 20_000],\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"Decision Tree\": {\n",
    "        \"model__max_depth\": [None, 5, 10, 15, 20, 30],\n",
    "        \"model__min_samples_split\": [2, 5, 10, 20],\n",
    "        \"model__min_samples_leaf\": [1, 2, 4, 8],\n",
    "        \"model__max_features\": [None, \"sqrt\", \"log2\"],\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"Random Forest\": {\n",
    "        \"model__n_estimators\": [200, 300, 500, 700],\n",
    "        \"model__max_depth\": [None, 8, 12, 16, 24],\n",
    "        \"model__min_samples_split\": [2, 5, 10],\n",
    "        \"model__min_samples_leaf\": [1, 2, 4],\n",
    "        \"model__max_features\": [None, \"sqrt\", \"log2\"],\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"Gradient Boosting\": {\n",
    "        \"model__n_estimators\": [100, 200, 300, 500],\n",
    "        \"model__learning_rate\": [0.01, 0.03, 0.05, 0.1, 0.2],\n",
    "        \"model__max_depth\": [2, 3, 4, 5],\n",
    "        \"model__min_samples_split\": [2, 5, 10],\n",
    "        \"model__min_samples_leaf\": [1, 2, 4],\n",
    "        \"model__subsample\": [0.7, 0.85, 1.0],\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"XGBoost\": {\n",
    "        \"model__n_estimators\": [200, 300, 500, 700],\n",
    "        \"model__learning_rate\": [0.01, 0.03, 0.05, 0.1, 0.2],\n",
    "        \"model__max_depth\": [3, 4, 5, 6, 8],\n",
    "        \"model__min_child_weight\": [1, 3, 5, 7],\n",
    "        \"model__subsample\": [0.7, 0.85, 1.0],\n",
    "        \"model__colsample_bytree\": [0.7, 0.85, 1.0],\n",
    "    },\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "top_two_models = (\n",
    "    baseline_results_df[\n",
    "        baseline_results_df[\"Model\"] != \"Dummy Median\"\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "    .head(2)[\"Model\"]\n",
    "    .tolist()\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Models selected for tuning:\")\n",
    "for name in top_two_models:\n",
    "    print(\"-\", name)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "12829567",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Hyperparameter Tuning"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "J1wR12valfUh",
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
     "height": 216
    },
    "id": "J1wR12valfUh",
    "outputId": "ac8f094a-1e41-4d2a-ab64-0f0358d654e9"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "tuned_models = {}\n",
    "tuning_results = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for model_name in top_two_models:\n",
    "    model_pipeline = Pipeline([\n",
    "        (\"preprocessor\", clone(preprocessor)),\n",
    "        (\"model\", clone(models[model_name])),\n",
    "    ])\n",
    "\n",
    "    param_distributions = search_spaces[model_name]\n",
    "    total_combinations = len(list(ParameterGrid(param_distributions)))\n",
    "    n_iter = min(20, total_combinations)\n",
    "\n",
    "    random_search = RandomizedSearchCV(\n",
    "        estimator=model_pipeline,\n",
    "        param_distributions=param_distributions,\n",
    "        n_iter=n_iter,\n",
    "        scoring=\"neg_root_mean_squared_error\",\n",
    "        cv=cv,\n",
    "        random_state=42,\n",
    "        n_jobs=-1,\n",
    "        refit=True,\n",
    "        verbose=1,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(\"\\nTuning:\", model_name)\n",
    "    random_search.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
    "\n",
    "    tuned_models[model_name] = random_search.best_estimator_\n",
    "\n",
    "    tuning_results.append({\n",
    "        \"Model\": model_name,\n",
    "        \"Best_CV_RMSE\": -random_search.best_score_,\n",
    "        \"Best_Params\": random_search.best_params_,\n",
    "    })\n",
    "\n",
    "tuning_results_df = (\n",
    "    pd.DataFrame(tuning_results)\n",
    "    .sort_values(\"Best_CV_RMSE\")\n",
    "    .reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "display(tuning_results_df)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "LZuJpzR-lfUi",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "LZuJpzR-lfUi"
   },
   "source": [
    "## 16. Raw Target vs Log Target — Training CV Only\n",
    "\n",
    "This closes the EDA question properly.\n",
    "\n",
    "We take the best tuned model structure and compare:\n",
    "\n",
    "- normal target: `selling_price`\n",
    "- log target: train on `log1p(selling_price)` and automatically transform predictions back with\n",
    "  `expm1`\n",
    "\n",
    "Both are evaluated in **original price units** with CV RMSE. The test set is still untouched.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "blIP7p7OlfUi",
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
     "height": 147
    },
    "id": "blIP7p7OlfUi",
    "outputId": "e8791d60-a77d-40f7-f3c8-7c4e05f068a9"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "best_model_name = tuning_results_df.loc[0, \"Model\"]\n",
    "best_raw_pipeline = tuned_models[best_model_name]\n",
    "\n",
    "raw_cv_scores = cross_validate(\n",
    "    clone(best_raw_pipeline),\n",
    "    X_train,\n",
    "    y_train,\n",
    "    cv=cv,\n",
    "    scoring={\n",
    "        \"rmse\": \"neg_root_mean_squared_error\",\n",
    "        \"r2\": \"r2\",\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    n_jobs=-1,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "log_target_model = TransformedTargetRegressor(\n",
    "    regressor=clone(best_raw_pipeline),\n",
    "    func=np.log1p,\n",
    "    inverse_func=np.expm1,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "log_cv_scores = cross_validate(\n",
    "    log_target_model,\n",
    "    X_train,\n",
    "    y_train,\n",
    "    cv=cv,\n",
    "    scoring={\n",
    "        \"rmse\": \"neg_root_mean_squared_error\",\n",
    "        \"r2\": \"r2\",\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    n_jobs=-1,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "raw_cv_rmse = -raw_cv_scores[\"test_rmse\"].mean()\n",
    "log_cv_rmse = -log_cv_scores[\"test_rmse\"].mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "raw_cv_r2 = raw_cv_scores[\"test_r2\"].mean()\n",
    "log_cv_r2 = log_cv_scores[\"test_r2\"].mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "target_comparison = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"Target Strategy\": [\"Raw selling_price\", \"Log1p selling_price\"],\n",
    "    \"CV_RMSE\": [raw_cv_rmse, log_cv_rmse],\n",
    "    \"CV_R2\": [raw_cv_r2, log_cv_r2],\n",
    "}).sort_values(\"CV_RMSE\")\n",
    "\n",
    "display(target_comparison.round(4))\n",
    "\n",
    "if log_cv_rmse < raw_cv_rmse:\n",
    "    selected_target_strategy = \"log1p\"\n",
    "    final_model = TransformedTargetRegressor(\n",
    "        regressor=clone(best_raw_pipeline),\n",
    "        func=np.log1p,\n",
    "        inverse_func=np.expm1,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    selected_target_strategy = \"raw\"\n",
    "    final_model = clone(best_raw_pipeline)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Selected model:\", best_model_name)\n",
    "print(\"Selected target strategy:\", selected_target_strategy)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "rEHP-ZdklfUi",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "rEHP-ZdklfUi"
   },
   "source": [
    "## 17. Final Test Evaluation\n",
    "\n",
    "Only now do we fit the selected final approach on all training rows and evaluate once on the held-out\n",
    "test set.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1C11yujVlfUj",
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
     "height": 244
    },
    "id": "1C11yujVlfUj",
    "outputId": "b2727193-e1e6-454e-f0da-ad2f40c31218"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "final_model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
    "y_pred = final_model.predict(X_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "test_mae = mean_absolute_error(y_test, y_pred)\n",
    "test_rmse = np.sqrt(mean_squared_error(y_test, y_pred))\n",
    "test_r2 = r2_score(y_test, y_pred)\n",
    "test_mape = mean_absolute_percentage_error(y_test, y_pred) * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "final_metrics = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"Metric\": [\"MAE\", \"RMSE\", \"R²\", \"MAPE (%)\"],\n",
    "    \"Value\": [test_mae, test_rmse, test_r2, test_mape],\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "display(final_metrics)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Final Test MAE : {test_mae:,.2f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Final Test RMSE: {test_rmse:,.2f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Final Test R²  : {test_r2:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Final Test MAPE: {test_mape:.2f}%\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "KwJF8buQlfUl",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "KwJF8buQlfUl"
   },
   "source": [
    "## 18. Dummy Test Baseline\n",
    "\n",
    "The Dummy model always predicts the training-set median. This gives the final model a concrete\n",
    "reference point on the same held-out test set.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "VgUiGf7UlfUm",
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
